ffuf
Usage: ffuf -u URL/FUZZ -w WORDLIST [-mc CODES] [-s]

Fast web fuzzer. It requests a URL over and over, putting each word from a
wordlist where you wrote `FUZZ`, and shows which ones answer -- the way you
find hidden paths, parameters or virtual hosts on a web target.

	-u URL/FUZZ   the target; `FUZZ` marks where each word is substituted
	-w WORDLIST   the words to try, one per line
	-mc CODES     keep only these HTTP status codes (e.g. -mc 200)
	-fc CODES     the opposite -- filter OUT these codes
	-s            quiet: just the hits, no banner or progress bar
	-t N          N requests at once (default 40)

Only ever against a site you own or are allowed to test. In this school the
target is always `127.0.0.1`. Pointed at a stranger's machine it is a crime,
not a drill.

See also: gobuster, httpx, nuclei
